<title>MEXICO: MEXICO JAN-JUNE ELECTRONICS EXPORTS EXCEED $22 BLN.</title>
<headline>MEXICO JAN-JUNE ELECTRONICS EXPORTS EXCEED $22 BLN.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's electronics industry exported goods worth more than $22 billion in the first half of 1997, the Trade and Industry Ministry (Secofi) said on Sunday.</p>
<p>The electronics industry accounted for four out of every ten dollars in export earnings, a statement by the Secofi added.</p>
<p>((-- Veronica Galan, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9553))</p>
